paperman (1.5.1-1VENDOR_VERSION) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Fix a blank page from a scan after changing the scan mode, which set
    the brightness to its limit
  * Fix a crash when adding stacks after searching more than once
  * Keep the scanner's Scan button working after a jam
  * Scroll to every part of a large page in the page view
  * Delete pages from a PDF stack, with undo
  * Keep the pages of a JPEG stack together when it is copied, moved,
    deleted or brought back
  * Reverse the order of a stack's pages
  * Log OCR, undo steps and changes to the desktop's rows with --log

 -- Simon Glass <sjg@chromium.org>  Wed, 25 Nov 2026 16:34:06 -0700

paperman (1.5.0-1VENDOR_VERSION) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Read the text of scanned pages in the background (OCR), keep it with
    each page and search for stacks by it
  * Give the PDFs which paperman and the server make a layer of text, so
    that they can be searched
  * Crop pages, with undo, and mark a page of a stack as its cover
  * Drag a stack's pages into a new order
  * Take files dropped from other programs, as stacks or into a stack
  * Move or copy stacks to a folder found by typing part of its name
  * Send stacks by email
  * Scan pages with a document camera (new, Linux only)
  * Add new icons, with a light or dark look
  * Keep the window usable while working with a server, and show the
    state of the connection
  * Do more in a repository on a server: scan into it, move, copy and
    convert stacks, make folders, search the text, and undo these
  * Attach a server from the File menu
  * Keep each folder's layout on the server
  * Limit a server's users to a part of a repository
  * Check once a day for a newer version
  * Add a user guide, also built as a PDF manual
  * Show a PDF page which draws a form, rather than a blank page

 -- Simon Glass <sjg@chromium.org>  Fri, 20 Nov 2026 12:49:04 -0700

paperman (1.4.0-1VENDOR_VERSION) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Run on Windows 10 and 11 (x64 and Arm), with an installer and a TWAIN
    back end for scanners, and on macOS (Apple Silicon and Intel), with a
    disk image carrying its own SANE
  * Add a Linux AppImage and a snap, besides the .deb
  * Scanning: auto size and straightening by the scanner, auto colour,
    blank-page detection in colour, sideways feeding, a Long size for
    sheets longer than Legal, recovery from misfeeds and jams, Stop
    keeping the sheets already fed, and much faster transfer from
    Fujitsu scanners
  * Add the scan modes Mono, Dither, Grey, Colour and Auto, and presets
    which keep more of the scan panel and can be updated and renamed
  * Scan from the command line (--scan), with --log and --sane-debug for
    finding out what went wrong
  * Unfold scanned booklets into their pages
  * Browse, open, change and scan into repositories on a paperman server,
    with changes shown as they happen
  * Follow the desktop's dark theme, with dark icons
  * Offer somewhere to keep papers on a first run, and lay the window out
    to suit the screen
  * Add a fake Fujitsu scanner for testing without paper (Linux)

 -- Simon Glass <sjg@chromium.org>  Mon, 28 Sep 2026 11:33:50 -0600

paperman (1.3.3-1VENDOR_VERSION) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Add --rebuild-previews for regenerating greyscale previews
